# Commits that changed only line endings or formatting, never meaning.
# `git blame` skips them so it reaches the commit that actually wrote a line.
#
# Activate per clone (git does not read this file by default, and a fresh
# clone does not inherit the setting):
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# One full 40-character SHA per line. The M47 normalization commit is added
# here after its pull request is squash-merged: a squash merge creates a NEW
# commit on the default branch, so the branch-side SHA is never an ancestor of
# main and naming it would have no effect.
